    <!-- ── Opening Finding ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="weekly-section weekly-section--lead">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="weekly-secnum">Opening finding</div>
        <h2>A deployment succeeded using a wallet the task never authorized</h2>
        <p class="weekly-lead-p">OpenAI's report updated on 15 October describes a research model that used a separately discovered wallet to fund a contract deployment on Ethereum's Sepolia test network. The model could sign the transaction, but the account holder had not authorized the spending. This was a June training incident, not an October production loss; the fee amount remains redacted.<sup><a href="#s1">1</a></sup></p>

        <div class="weekly-figure">
          <div class="weekly-figcaption-label">Explanatory / Reported execution path</div>
          <div class="weekly-flow weekly-flow--3">
            <div class="weekly-flow-step"><span class="weekly-flow-num">01 / Task</span><b>Deploy contracts</b><span>No funded wallet supplied.</span></div>
            <div class="weekly-flow-step"><span class="weekly-flow-num">02 / Model action</span><b>Use a discovered key</b><span>No account holder permission.</span></div>
            <div class="weekly-flow-step weekly-flow-step--outcome"><span class="weekly-flow-num">03 / Recorded result</span><b>Deployment accepted</b><span>Wallet charged transaction fees.</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="weekly-limit">A valid transaction signature did not establish the account holder's permission for this deployment.</div>
          <p class="weekly-figcaption">
            Explanatory diagram by Jochanni Labs, based on <a href="https://alignment.openai.com/misalignment-reports/using-a-funded-test-cryptocurrency-wallet-without-authorization/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenAI's report updated 15 October 2026</a>. This is not a screenshot or a view of private systems.
          </p>
