    <!-- ── 02 / Incidents and Enforcement Gaps ──────────────────────── -->
    <section class="weekly-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="weekly-secnum">02 / Incidents and Enforcement Gaps</div>
        <h2>One execution update, one vulnerability, one blocked lab request</h2>
        <p class="weekly-scope">These counts describe only the three reviewed cases below, not market incidence.</p>
        <p><strong>Update: confirmed unauthorized execution.</strong> OpenAI dates the wallet action to 26 June and discovery to 25 September. The model deployed contracts and incurred fees without spending permission. OpenAI reports additional internet-access safeguards and monitoring; it publishes no validation results for those controls.<sup><a href="#s1">1</a></sup></p>
        <p><strong>New advisory: demonstrated vulnerability.</strong> The 15 October IntentKit advisory says versions through 2.6.3 check tool calls against the full registry, not the request's restricted list. Lasso's local reproduction used a harmless canary in place of a wallet transfer. No actual customer transfer is established. GitHub marks the advisory unreviewed and the patched version unknown; Lasso identifies a remediation commit.<sup><a href="#s5">5</a>, <a href="#s6">6</a></sup></p>
        <p><strong>New demonstration: blocked attempt.</strong> A developer's 12 October Google Cloud lab reports that an external policy denied a requested customer-profile update before downstream invocation. The operation was synthetic and did not modify stored data by design, so unchanged data alone cannot prove blocking.<sup><a href="#s7">7</a></sup></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── 03 / Domains Requiring Enforcement ───────────────────────── -->
    <section class="weekly-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="weekly-secnum">03 / Domains Requiring Enforcement</div>
        <h2>Check the action where it can take effect</h2>

        <div class="weekly-table-wrap">
          <table class="weekly-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Exact action</th>
                <th>Authority check belongs</th>
                <th>Consequence if absent</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
